```matlab
pressureReading = readVoltage(a, ANALOG_INPUT_PIN)*1.55;
addpoints(h1, toc(timetracker), pressureReading);
addpoints(h, volume, pressureReading);
fprintf(FID,'%10.3f %10.3f %10.3f \r\n',toc(timerecord),volume,pressureReading);
```
This excerpt from my control and data acquisition code shows analog signal acquisition, live pressure plotting, pressure-volume plotting, and timestamped data logging.

The 1.55 multiplier is the calibration factor converting analog sensor voltage to kPa. The %10.3f fields are time, volume, and pressure.
